    "Le maximum, et la pression forte s'ouvre.":"The maximum, and high boost opens up.",
    "VOLANT MOTEUR":"FLYWHEEL",
    "Plus nerveux. Reprend un peu moins bien.":"Livelier. Pulls back a little less well.",
    "Tres nerveux, et cale facilement.":"Very lively, and stalls easily.",
    "GRAISSAGE":"LUBRICATION",
    "MELANGE":"PREMIX",
    "Huile dans l'essence. Simple, approximatif.":"Oil in the fuel. Simple, approximate.",
    "GRAISSAGE SEPARE":"SEPARATE OILING",
    "Dose selon la charge.":"Metered according to load.",
    "HUILE COMPETITION":"RACING OIL",
    "Tient les pleins gaz prolonges.":"Holds up to sustained full throttle.",
    "ATMOSPHERIQUE":"NATURALLY ASPIRATED",
    "Reponse immediate. Sur un moteur deja suralimente, c'est une DEPOSE : la pression s'en va, la puissance avec.":"Instant response. On an already forced-induction engine this is a REMOVAL: the boost goes, and the power with it.",
    "Du couple des le bas, sans aucun temps de reponse. Il se paye : le vilebrequin l'entraine.":"Torque from low down, with no lag at all. It has a price: the crankshaft drives it.",
    "Le meme, plus fort et plus lourd.":"The same, stronger and heavier.",
    "Le plus gros gain a la pression, avec un temps de reponse.":"The biggest gain for the boost, with some lag.",
    "Deux turbines en parallele : plus de pression, moins d'attente.":"Two turbines in parallel: more boost, less waiting.",
    "BI-TURBO SEQUENTIEL":"SEQUENTIAL TWIN-TURBO",
    "Une petite puis une grosse : le trou est comble.":"A small one then a big one: the hole is filled.",
    "Le bas du compresseur, le haut du turbo.":"The supercharger's bottom end, the turbo's top end.",
    "PRESSION DE SURALIMENTATION":"BOOST PRESSURE",
